  "id": "Compound::DB00284 - Gene::276",
  "verbalization": "Acarbose exhibits a strong, consistent interaction with Amy1a, as evidenced by three distinct paths in the hetionet dataset. All three paths indicate that Acarbose binds to Amy1b, which then participates in the Amylase Activity, ultimately leading to Amy1a being involved in this process. The binding of Acarbose to Amy1b suggests a direct interaction that may inhibit the enzymatic activity of Amy1a. The high scores across the three paths (0.7705, 0.7624, and 0.744) indicate a robust and reliable relationship, supported by multiple independent pathways. The mechanism appears to involve Acarbose acting as a competitive inhibitor of Amy1b, thereby modulating the activity of Amy1a. This relationship is further supported by the presence of a shared pathway involving Amylase Activity, suggesting a coordinated regulatory role in carbohydrate metabolism. The integration of these findings supports a mechanistic link between Acarbose and Amy1a, emphasizing the importance of Amy1b in the enzymatic cascade leading to Amy1a's function.",
